[{:db/id "01e8aae2-003e-59d4-9f51-6280d59e1f6d" :answer/id #uuid "01e8aae2-003e-59d4-9f51-6280d59e1f6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b81326d1-592e-5dc9-ace3-bf8cccf3c8ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "b81326d1-592e-5dc9-ace3-bf8cccf3c8ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["01e8aae2-003e-59d4-9f51-6280d59e1f6d"] :answer-field/correct "01e8aae2-003e-59d4-9f51-6280d59e1f6d" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "4d8a6047-d4db-5e7d-bc35-ab461c2bccd5" :answer/id #uuid "4d8a6047-d4db-5e7d-bc35-ab461c2bccd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "df8790b5-8bb3-538f-a840-1ca0e2d1db38" :answer-field/id #uuid "df8790b5-8bb3-538f-a840-1ca0e2d1db38" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["4d8a6047-d4db-5e7d-bc35-ab461c2bccd5"] :answer-field/correct "4d8a6047-d4db-5e7d-bc35-ab461c2bccd5" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "014ba384-9efa-58d4-8e01-62ced760018d" :question/id #uuid "014ba384-9efa-58d4-8e01-62ced760018d" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-8t,\\,y=-{t}^{3}-6{t}^{2}-9t,\\,-\\infty<t<\\infty.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if $y'(t)=0$ while $x'(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx'(t)={t}^{2}-2t-8,\\qquad y'(t)=-3{t}^{2}-12t-9.\n$$\n\nSolving $y'(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{t}^{2}-12t-9 & =0 \\\\ -3(t+1)(t+3) & =0 \\\\ t & =-3,-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(-3) & =7\\ne 0, \\\\ x'(-1) & =-5\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=-3$ and $t=-1$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["b81326d1-592e-5dc9-ace3-bf8cccf3c8ec" "df8790b5-8bb3-538f-a840-1ca0e2d1db38"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "90dab570-d4d5-5d14-95e8-cf430ba68a9c" :answer/id #uuid "90dab570-d4d5-5d14-95e8-cf430ba68a9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f369480f-edf6-52d7-aeb5-a7f4d6b2804a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f369480f-edf6-52d7-aeb5-a7f4d6b2804a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["90dab570-d4d5-5d14-95e8-cf430ba68a9c"] :answer-field/correct "90dab570-d4d5-5d14-95e8-cf430ba68a9c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "449eb05f-0eb9-526c-953c-ff1dcf5569bf" :answer/id #uuid "449eb05f-0eb9-526c-953c-ff1dcf5569bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9e4d6224-315e-5264-ae6c-6736bd08b681" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e4d6224-315e-5264-ae6c-6736bd08b681" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["449eb05f-0eb9-526c-953c-ff1dcf5569bf"] :answer-field/correct "449eb05f-0eb9-526c-953c-ff1dcf5569bf" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d4f121dc-20d5-5eda-9d00-aee680d617e5" :question/id #uuid "d4f121dc-20d5-5eda-9d00-aee680d617e5" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+12t,\\,y={t}^{3}-\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-6t,\\,-\\infty<t<\\infty.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if $y'(t)=0$ while $x'(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=-2{t}^{2}+2t+12,\\qquad y'(t)=3{t}^{2}-3t-6.\n$$\n\nSolving $y'(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}-3t-6 & =0 \\\\ 3(t-2)(t+1) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(-1) & =8\\ne 0, \\\\ x'(2) & =8\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=-1$ and $t=2$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["f369480f-edf6-52d7-aeb5-a7f4d6b2804a" "9e4d6224-315e-5264-ae6c-6736bd08b681"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "101c6d23-9011-58fd-9edb-d075ec501e2e" :answer/id #uuid "101c6d23-9011-58fd-9edb-d075ec501e2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bf995db9-cac7-5062-9da3-ca1256276995" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf995db9-cac7-5062-9da3-ca1256276995" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["101c6d23-9011-58fd-9edb-d075ec501e2e"] :answer-field/correct "101c6d23-9011-58fd-9edb-d075ec501e2e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "2e3aefa0-3c97-5c28-89c2-9c4da8965c43" :answer/id #uuid "2e3aefa0-3c97-5c28-89c2-9c4da8965c43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3239d979-9412-599c-bf13-cf6040c94d87" :answer-field/id #uuid "3239d979-9412-599c-bf13-cf6040c94d87" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["2e3aefa0-3c97-5c28-89c2-9c4da8965c43"] :answer-field/correct "2e3aefa0-3c97-5c28-89c2-9c4da8965c43" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "6ec681ae-b1cb-54f1-95d3-8f457841921f" :question/id #uuid "6ec681ae-b1cb-54f1-95d3-8f457841921f" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}-6t,\\,y=-2{t}^{3}+18{t}^{2}-48t,\\,-\\infty<t<\\infty.\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is horizontal if $y'(t)=0$ while $x'(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\nx'(t)=-2{t}^{2}-8t-6,\\qquad y'(t)=-6{t}^{2}+36t-48.\n$$\n\nSolving $y'(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{t}^{2}+36t-48 & =0 \\\\ -6(t-4)(t-2) & =0 \\\\ t & =2,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x'(2) & =-30\\ne 0, \\\\ x'(4) & =-70\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that the tangent to the curve is indeed horizontal at $t=2$ and $t=4$." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["bf995db9-cac7-5062-9da3-ca1256276995" "3239d979-9412-599c-bf13-cf6040c94d87"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8f496004-c77c-54f4-b7db-0caedac3bca7" :answer/id #uuid "8f496004-c77c-54f4-b7db-0caedac3bca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c4e1ea25-fbba-5fba-acdb-34806cf4fd41" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4e1ea25-fbba-5fba-acdb-34806cf4fd41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["8f496004-c77c-54f4-b7db-0caedac3bca7"] :answer-field/correct "8f496004-c77c-54f4-b7db-0caedac3bca7" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d6862b69-924c-5bfb-b51c-6174266c9ded" :answer/id #uuid "d6862b69-924c-5bfb-b51c-6174266c9ded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7877e8a5-ece2-5b45-a09e-866686e5f391" :answer-field/id #uuid "7877e8a5-ece2-5b45-a09e-866686e5f391" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/choices ["d6862b69-924c-5bfb-b51c-61742